      "inspected_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor": "The canonical Python repository is py-why/EconML. The selected pre-cutoff commit declares version 0.17.0; the README records its 31 July 2026 release. These are distinct from authentication of a release wheel.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The pinned root license contains MIT conditions and BSD 3-Clause notices for scikit-learn-derived tree/grf code. Python >=3.9, eleven direct dependency declarations, optional extras and native build requirements are recorded; they do not constitute a resolved environment or complete transitive rights audit.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The selected DML documentation and R-learner code residualize Y and treatment using X and W, then fit an effect function of X. Causal interpretation needs the stated identifying assumptions and effect-model specification.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The final linear path fits cross-products of features and treatment residuals. The alternative weighted path divides by signed treatment residuals clipped at 1e-5 and weights by the original squared residual. This numerical convention cannot create overlap.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The base ate API averages predicted effect over supplied X and contrasts; averaging a misspecified constant projection does not transform it into a correctly specified population effect.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Group labels control cross-fitting splits. cv=1 disables cross-fitting. The inspected static linear covariance supports HC0, HC1 and nonrobust options and warns when rank deficiency invalidates inference; it does not automatically supply clustered or calendar covariance.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "DynamicDML counts periods by occurrence within each group, requires equal group counts, uses baseline X for heterogeneity and later X as controls, and targets the final-period outcome in the inspected nuisance path. Its warning explicitly says supplied sample_weight and sample_var are ignored.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The dynamic documentation assumes fully observed dynamic confounders and a specified structural family; it does not establish an arbitrary latent-state policy-value result. Backward treatment residual fitting and cross-period within-unit covariance are visible in the selected implementation.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The dynamic covariance assembles within-unit cross-period score products and divides by the number of groups. This is distinct from qualifying cross-unit common-calendar dependence.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The inspected call chain maps bootstrap inference to BootstrapEstimator.fit, takes DynamicDML._strata=groups, and resamples rows with replacement separately inside each fixed group. The row sequence can duplicate or reorder periods under the encounter-order convention. This is a source composition finding, not a fresh native execution or measured coverage defect.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The inspected upstream dynamic tests include shape/inference cases with two bootstrap draws and selected order-preserving panel layouts under auto inference. Bootstrap tests include interval shapes, internal options and treatment stratification. They were read, not executed; these selected tests do not establish the proposed whole-history resampling contract.",
          "inspection": "Authenticated primary implementation/documentation"
        }
      ],
